hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15605","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah, from Hanzalah ibn Qays al-Zuraqi, from Abi al-Yasar, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, shade him in His shade, let him give respite to one in hardship, or remit from him."
"15606","Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, and Muawiyah ibn Amr said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi, he said: Abu al-Yasar narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits from him, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will shade him in His shade. Muawiyah said: On a day when there is no shade except His shade."
"15607","Harun ibn Maruf and Surayj and Muawiyah ibn Amr said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari, from Abi al-Yasar, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among you is one who prays the prayer complete, and among you is one who prays half, and a third, and a quarter, until he reached a tenth. Surayj said in his hadith: until he reached a tenth."
"15608","Makki ibn Ibrahim said: Abdullah ibn Said, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, narrated to us, from Sayfi, the freed slave of Aflah, the freed slave of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from Abi al-Yasar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate with these seven words, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from extreme old age, and I seek refuge in You from falling from a height, and I seek refuge in You from grief and drowning and burning and old age, and I seek refuge in You that Satan confound me at death, and I seek refuge in You from dying in Your path turning back, and I seek refuge in You from dying stung."
"15609","Ali ibn Bahr said: Abu Damrah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Said narrated to me, from his grandfather Abu Hind, from Sayfi, from Abi al-Yasar al-Sulami, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from destruction and falling and old age and drowning and burning, and I seek refuge in You that Satan confound me at death, and that I be killed in Your path turning back, and that I die stung."
"15610","It was recited to Yaqub in the military expeditions of his father, from Ibn Ishaq. Ibn Ishaq said: Buraydah ibn Sufyan al-Aslami narrated to me, from some men of Banu Salamah, from Abi al-Yasar Kab ibn Amr, he said: He said: By Allah, we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Khaybar in the evening, when some sheep of a Jewish man came heading for their fortress, while we were besieging them, when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who is a man who will feed us from these sheep. Abu al-Yasar said: So I said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then do it. He said: So I went out running like an ostrich, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me going, he said: O Allah, let us enjoy him. He said: So I caught up with the sheep after the first of them had entered the fortress, so I took two sheep from the last of them and held them under my arms, then I came with them running as if there was nothing with me, until I laid them before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they slaughtered them and ate them. Abu al-Yasar was among the last of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to die, and when he narrated this hadith he wept, then he would say: Enjoy me, by my life, I was the last of them."
